.TH SDL_JoystickConnectionState 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_JoystickConnectionState \- Possible connection states for a joystick device.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_joystick.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef enum SDL_JoystickConnectionState
.BI "{
.BI "    SDL_JOYSTICK_CONNECTION_INVALID = -1,
.BI "    SDL_JOYSTICK_CONNECTION_UNKNOWN,
.BI "    SDL_JOYSTICK_CONNECTION_WIRED,
.BI "    SDL_JOYSTICK_CONNECTION_WIRELESS
.BI "} SDL_JoystickConnectionState;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This is used by
.BR SDL_GetJoystickConnectionState
to report how a device is connected to the system\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This enum is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

